A||N||12||Elenor84||How do I replace my water pump belt?||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||12-26-2001||01:23 AM||||Hey guys...I finished replacing my lower rad hose today but the system still over heated...on further inspection I had no waterpump belt...how do I replace it...tools techniques?  Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-26-2001||05:14 PM||||if its a V6 theres one belt for only AC, one for all the rest. Water pump, alternator, crank are all together.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||12-28-2001||12:41 AM||||o ya...sorry its a 4 cylinder...hanes manual is a bit iffy...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Posthumane||12-28-2001||02:30 AM||||The alternator acts as a tensioner (sort of), so you have to loosen it off. Loosening the bolt at the top of the alternator will allow it to move back and forth. Move it forward as far as it will go, put the belt on around the w/p, alt, and crank pulleys, and then use a pry bar to put the alternator back to the desired position to keep the belt at the right tension, and tighten the bolt at the top of the alt. Having a partner to help you with this makes it easier, cuz one can hold the pry bar while the other tightens the bolt.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroman_5000||12-28-2001||11:06 AM||||what about the one that goes aroung the AC on a 4 banger...there is no alternator there? <P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-28-2001||02:44 PM||||you adjust the AC one by loosening the compressor and pulling it, just like alternator.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Elenor84||12-28-2001||10:17 PM||||Alright guys...here I go!  wish me luck...its -15 out here so I'm going to freeze my butt off but it'll all be worth it having my baby back...I'll get back to u as soon as I'm done...and thx alot for the reply's...gave about 10 times as much info as the hanes manual...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Elenor84||12-28-2001||11:53 PM||||Ok...I losened the bolt to the alt but its still not enough..I can't get htis stupid belt on!~!!!!!!  Now, there are two slots on the crankshaft pully and the water pump pully...witch one do I put it on?  The one closer to the engine or the one further away?  Any tips guys/???  I've used flat head screw driver and I've tryed everything...;I need to get this stupid thing on...any advice would be great...thx!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Elenor84||12-29-2001||12:22 AM||||Please guys...I really need some help...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||avengador1||12-29-2001||06:11 PM||||Make sure you loosen both bolts on the alternator or it won't be "loose". You will know when it is loose as you should be able to just slip the belt on easily. Unless you have the wrong size belt to begin with.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieroman_5000||12-29-2001||09:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>you adjust the AC one by loosening the compressor and pulling it, just like alternator.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks...now i don't have to spend half an hour trying to stretch it over...lol<P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||fieroman_5000||12-29-2001||09:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR><B>Please guys...I really need some help...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>heres how it is on mine...the belt that goes from crank to w/p, alt is the one closest to the block. while the ac is the outer one. Hopes thins helps!<P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Return of Fiero||12-31-2001||11:44 AM||||I know AC and Non-AC engines will be different, but on my 88's there was a tentioner pully, and with a breaker bar in the slot on the pully arm, I was able to pull back the tentioner far enough to put on and take off belts with ease. I never had to losen anything. I just pryed back the tentioner, and pulled off the old belt, then pryed it back and put on the new belt. Is an AC system THAT much different that the pump belt doesnt have a tentioner?<P>Later Gator,<BR>Myke||||reg||1
